{
    "background_story": "Gigi was a talented calligrapher and artist who lived in a small village surrounded by ancient ruins. She spent most of her days exploring the crumbling temples and studying the intricate inscriptions that adorned the walls. Gigi was fascinated by the stories these inscriptions told and the secrets they held. She became determined to preserve the ancient language and art form by inscribing the texts onto handmade paper and vellum. As her skills improved, Gigi began to receive commissions from collectors and scholars who sought her expertise. She spent years inscribing ancient texts, including a rare copy of the village's founding charter. Gigi's work not only preserved the village's history but also brought her a sense of purpose and connection to the past.",
